"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nIt explains events that seem interpretable only supernaturally and mystically, such as premonitory dreams, out-of-body experiences, and poltergeists, through the scientific principles of .  \n\nBeyond simply revealing tricks, it poses the fundamental question of how superstition and science coexist and conflict in modern society.  \n\nIt explains different mysteries and the scientific principles applied to them in five independent short stories.  \n\nThe author seems to encourage the habit of doubting phenomena rather than blindly believing them, and thinking logically.  "